  "body": [
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_1"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ayaṃ duḥkhavrātavrataparigame pāraṇavidhir",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "mahāsaukhyāsāraprasaraṇarase durdinam idam |",
              "segment_number": 2,
              "translated_text": "this is the cloudy day in the flowing delight of the downpour of supreme bliss —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 1,
          "translated_text": "This [hymn] is the completion-rite (<s>pāraṇa</s>) at the end of the observance (<s>vrata</s>) that is the multitude of sorrows;"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yad anyanyakkṛtyā viṣamaviśikhaploṣaṇaguror vibhoḥ stotre",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "śaśvat pratiphalati ceto gatabhayam ||",
              "segment_number": 4,
              "translated_text": "the mind rests perpetually, free from fear. || 1 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 3,
          "translated_text": "since, through the power of transforming [all things], in the hymn to the Lord who is mighty in scorching [the world with his] terrible arrows,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_2"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vimṛśya svātmānaṃ vimṛśati punaḥ stutyacaritaṃ tathā",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "stotā stotre prakaṭayati bhedaikaviṣaye |",
              "segment_number": 6,
              "translated_text": "the praiser, in the hymn, reveals [the Self] which has differentiation as its sole domain;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 5,
          "translated_text": "Having reflected upon one's own Self, one again reflects on the deeds of the one to be praised; thus"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vimṛṣṭaś ca svātmā nikhilaviṣayajñānasamaye taditthaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "tvatstotre 'ham iha satataṃ yatnarahitaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 8,
              "translated_text": "in your hymn, I am here perpetually, free from effort. || 2 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 7,
          "translated_text": "and the Self, having been reflected upon, at the time of knowledge of all objects — therefore, thus:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_3"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "anāmṛṣṭaḥ svātmā na hi bhavati bhāvapramitibhāj anāmṛṣṭaḥ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "svātmety api hi na vinā 'marśanavidheḥ |",
              "segment_number": 10,
              "translated_text": "even this [thought] is not [possible] without the act of reflective awareness (<s>āmarśana</s>);"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 9,
          "translated_text": "Indeed, the Self that is not reflected upon (<s>anāmṛṣṭa</s>) does not become the cognizer of entities; 'the Self is not reflected upon' —"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "śivaś cāsau svātmā sphurad akhilabhāvaikasarasas tato 'ham",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "tvatstotre pravaṇahṛdayo nityasukhitaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 12,
              "translated_text": "in your hymn, am with an inclined heart, eternally blissful. || 3 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 11,
          "translated_text": "and this Self is <s>Śiva</s>, flashing forth, the sole essence of all entities — therefore I,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_4"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vicitrair jātyādibhramaṇaparipāṭīparikarair avāptam",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "sārvajñaṃ hṛdaya yad ayatnena bhavatā |",
              "segment_number": 14,
              "translated_text": "O heart, that omniscience (<s>sārvajña</s>) which was attained by you without effort —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 13,
          "translated_text": "Through the varied accessories of the successive course of wandering in births and the like,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tad antas tvadbodhaprasarasaraṇībhūtamahasi sphuṭam vāci",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "prāpya prakaṭaya vibhoḥ stotram adhunā ||",
              "segment_number": 16,
              "translated_text": "having attained clarity in speech, now reveal the hymn of the Lord! || 4 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 15,
          "translated_text": "that, within the radiance which has become the path for the expansion of your knowledge,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_5"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vidhunvāno bandhābhimatabhavamārgasthitim imāṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "rasīkṛtyānantastutihutavahaploṣitabhedām |",
              "segment_number": 18,
              "translated_text": "having savored it, with all differentiation burnt away by the fire of infinite praise,"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 17,
          "translated_text": "Shaking off this abiding in the path of worldly existence (<s>bhava</s>) which is deemed bondage,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vicitrasvasphārasphuritamahimārambharabhasāt piban bhāvān",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "etān varada madamatto 'smi sukhitaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 20,
              "translated_text": "drinking in these entities, O Granter of Boons (<s>Varada</s>), I am intoxicated with joy, blissful! || 5 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 19,
          "translated_text": "from the impetus of the onset of glory flashing forth in variegated self-expansion —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_6"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhava prājyaiśvaryaprathitabahuśakter bhagavato vicitraṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "cāritraṃ hṛdayam adhiśete yadi tataḥ |",
              "segment_number": 22,
              "translated_text": "with abundant sovereignty, pervades the heart — then"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 21,
          "translated_text": "If the wonderful activity of the Lord (<s>Bhagavat</s>), whose many <s>śaktis</s> (powers) are renowned"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "kathaṃ stotraṃ kuryād atha ca kurute tena sahasā",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "śivaikātmyaprāptau śivanatir upāyaḥ prathamakaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 24,
              "translated_text": "obeisance to <s>Śiva</s> is the primary means for attaining oneness with <s>Śiva</s>. || 6 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 23,
          "translated_text": "how could one compose a hymn? And yet one does compose it — therefore, suddenly,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_7"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "jvaladrūpaṃ bhāsvatpacanam atha dāhaṃ prakaṭanam",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "vimucyānyad vahneḥ kim api ghaṭate naiva hi vapuḥ |",
              "segment_number": 26,
              "translated_text": "apart from [these], no other body of fire whatsoever is ever produced;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 25,
          "translated_text": "The blazing form, the luminous cooking, the manifest burning —"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "stuve saṃvidraśmīn yadi nijanijāṃs tena sa nuto bhaven",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "nānyaḥ kaścid bhavati parameśasya vibhavaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 28,
              "translated_text": "no other glory of the Supreme Lord (<s>Parameśa</s>) exists [apart from consciousness]. || 7 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 27,
          "translated_text": "if I praise the rays of consciousness (<s>saṃvid</s>), which are his very own, then by that he is praised —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_8"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vicitrārambhatve galitaniyame yaḥ kila rasaḥ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "paricchedābhāvāt paramaparipūrṇatvam asamam |",
              "segment_number": 30,
              "translated_text": "due to the absence of limitation — unsurpassed, supreme fullness;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 29,
          "translated_text": "That delight (<s>rasa</s>) which, in the variety of beginnings, is free from all regulation;"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "svayaṃ bhāsāṃ yogaḥ sakalabhavabhāvaikamayatāviruddhair",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "dharmaughaiḥ paracitir anarghocitaguṇā ||",
              "segment_number": 32,
              "translated_text": "[together] with contradictory streams of properties, the supreme awareness (<s>paraciti</s>), endowed with priceless and fitting qualities. || 8 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 31,
          "translated_text": "the self-luminous union, the sole essence of all entities of existence —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_9"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "itīdṛkṣair rūpair varada vividhaṃ te kila vapur vibhāti",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "svāṃśe 'smin jagati gatabhedaṃ bhagavataḥ |",
              "segment_number": 34,
              "translated_text": "in this world which is a portion of your own [being], beyond differentiation, O Lord;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 33,
          "translated_text": "Thus, O Granter of Boons, with such forms your manifold body shines forth,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tad evaitatstotuṃ hṛdayam atha gīrbāhyakaraṇaprabandhāś ca",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "syur me satatam aparityaktarabhasaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 36,
              "translated_text": "be mine forever, with unabandoned fervor! || 9 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 35,
          "translated_text": "that very [body] — to praise this, may my heart, and the chain of speech, external organs,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_10"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tavaivaikasyāntaḥ sphuritamahaso bodhajaladher",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "vicitrormivrātaprasaraṇaraso yaḥ svarasataḥ |",
              "segment_number": 38,
              "translated_text": "that delight of the outpouring of multitudes of varied waves, arising spontaneously;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 37,
          "translated_text": "Of you alone, the one, the ocean of awareness (<s>bodha</s>) whose radiance flashes within —"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ta evāmī sṛṣṭisthitilayamayasphūrjitarucāṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "śaśāṅkārkāgnīnāṃ yugapad udayāpāyavibhavāḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 40,
              "translated_text": "of the moon, sun, and fire — the glories of simultaneous arising and dissolution. || 10 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 39,
          "translated_text": "these very ones are [the glory] of the flashing forth as creation (<s>sṛṣṭi</s>), maintenance (<s>sthiti</s>), and dissolution (<s>laya</s>),"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_11"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ataś citrācitrakramataditarādisthitijuṣo vibhoḥ śaktiḥ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "śaśvad vrajati na vibhedaṃ katham api |",
              "segment_number": 42,
              "translated_text": "never undergoes differentiation in any way;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 41,
          "translated_text": "Therefore, the <s>śakti</s> (power) of the Lord, who abides in the succession of the varied and the unvaried and the others,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tad etasyāṃ bhūmāv akulam iti te yat kila padaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "tadekāgrībhūyān mama hṛdayabhūr bhairava vibho ||",
              "segment_number": 44,
              "translated_text": "may that become the one-pointed ground of my heart, O <s>Bhairava</s>, O Lord! || 11 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 43,
          "translated_text": "therefore, on this ground, that state of yours which is called <s>Akula</s> (beyond the group) —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_12"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "amuṣmāt saṃpūrnāt vata rasamahollāsasarasān nijāṃ śaktiṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bhedaṃ gamayasi nijecchāprasarataḥ |",
              "segment_number": 46,
              "translated_text": "you cause to undergo differentiation by the expansion of your own will (<s>icchā</s>);"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 45,
          "translated_text": "From that fullness, ah! — moist with the great delight of aesthetic rapture (<s>rasa</s>) — your own <s>śakti</s> (power),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "anarghaṃ svātantryaṃ tava tadidam atyadbhutamayīṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bhavacchaktiṃ stunvan vigalitabhayo 'haṃ śivamayaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 48,
              "translated_text": "<s>śakti</s> of yours, I, free from fear, am one with <s>Śiva</s>. || 12 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 47,
          "translated_text": "that priceless independence (<s>svātantrya</s>) of yours — praising this most wondrous"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_13"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "idantāvad rūpaṃ tava bhagavataḥ śaktisarasaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "kramābhāvād eva prasabhavigalat kālakalanam |",
              "segment_number": 50,
              "translated_text": "due to the very absence of succession, forcefully dissolving the movement of time —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 49,
          "translated_text": "This form of 'this-ness' (<s>idantā</s>) of yours, O Lord, which is moist with <s>śakti</s>,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "manaḥśaktyā vācāpy atha karaṇacakrair bahir atho ghaṭādyais",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "tadrūpaṃ yugapad adhitiṣṭheyam aniśam ||",
              "segment_number": 52,
              "translated_text": "may I constantly abide in that form simultaneously [at all levels]! || 13 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 51,
          "translated_text": "through the power of mind (<s>manas</s>), through speech (<s>vāc</s>), then through the circle of sense-organs (<s>karaṇacakra</s>) externally, and then through pots and the like —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_14"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "kramollāsaṃ tasyāṃ bhuvi viracayan bhedakalanāṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "svaśaktīnāṃ deva prathayasi sadā svātmani tataḥ |",
              "segment_number": 54,
              "translated_text": "of your own powers (<s>śaktis</s>), O God, you ever manifest within your own Self; therefore,"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 53,
          "translated_text": "Producing on that ground the unfolding in succession, the articulation of differentiation"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "kriyājñānecchākhyāṃ sthitilayamahāsṛṣṭivibhavāṃ trirūpaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bhūyāsaṃ samadhiśayituṃ vyagrahṛdayaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 56,
              "translated_text": "may I become [one who is] eager-hearted to encompass [them]! || 14 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 55,
          "translated_text": "the threefold form called action (<s>kriyā</s>), knowledge (<s>jñāna</s>), and will (<s>icchā</s>), whose glory is maintenance, dissolution, and great creation —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_15"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "purā sṛṣṭir līnā hutavahamayī yātra vilaset",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "parollāsaunmukhyaṃ vrajati śaśisaṃsparśasubhagā |",
              "segment_number": 58,
              "translated_text": "[and] becomes inclined toward the highest bliss, beautiful with the touch of the moon —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 57,
          "translated_text": "Where the creation, formerly dissolved, blazes forth as fire (<s>hutavaha</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "hutāśendusphārobhayavibhavabhāg bhairavavibho taveyaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "sṛṣṭyākhyā mama manasi nityaṃ vilasatām ||",
              "segment_number": 60,
              "translated_text": "may this [<s>śakti</s>] of yours called Creation (<s>Sṛṣṭi</s>) shine perpetually in my mind! || 15 ||"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 59,
          "translated_text": "O <s>Bhairava</s>, O Lord, [the creation] which partakes of the glory of both the expansion of fire and the expansion of the moon —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_16"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "visṛṣṭe bhāvāṃśe bahir atiśayāsvādavirase yadā",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "tatraiva tvaṃ bhajasi rabhasād raktimayatām |",
              "segment_number": 62,
              "translated_text": "when you, right there, assume with fervor the nature of attachment (<s>rakti</s>),"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 61,
          "translated_text": "When the portion of entities has been emitted outward, in the delight of supreme relish,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tadā raktā devī tava sakalabhāveṣu nanu māṃ kriyād",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "raktāpānakramaghaṭitagoṣṭhīgataghṛṇam ||",
              "segment_number": 64,
              "translated_text": "having abandoned shame in the assembly formed by the sequence of drinking blood."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 63,
          "translated_text": "then your Goddess <s>Raktā</s> (the Attached/Red One), in all entities, surely [would embrace] me —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_17"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bahir vṛttiṃ hātuṃ citibhuvam udārāṃ nivasituṃ yadā",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bhāvābhedaṃ prathayasi vinaṣṭormicapalaḥ |",
              "segment_number": 66,
              "translated_text": "you manifest the non-difference of [all] states — the waves' restlessness having ceased —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 65,
          "translated_text": "When, in order to abandon outward activity and to dwell in the expansive ground of consciousness (<s>citibhūmi</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "sthiter nāśaṃ devī kalayati tadā sā tava vibho sthiteḥ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "sāṃsārikyāḥ kalayatu vināśaṃ mama sadā ||",
              "segment_number": 68,
              "translated_text": "always effect the destruction of my <s>saṃsāric</s> (worldly) stability."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 67,
          "translated_text": "the Goddess then effects the destruction of stability, O Lord; may she, [the destroyer] of stability,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_18"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "jagatsaṃhāreṇa praśamayitukāmaḥ svarabhasāt",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "svaśaṅkātaṅkākhyaṃ vidhim atha niṣedhaṃ prathayasi |",
              "segment_number": 70,
              "translated_text": "you manifest first the injunction called 'one's own doubt and fear' and then the prohibition;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 69,
          "translated_text": "Desiring to pacify by the dissolution of the world, impelled by your own momentum,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yamaṃ sṛṣṭvetthaṃ tvaṃ punar api ca śaṅkāṃ vidalayan",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "mahādevī seyaṃ mama bhavabhayaṃ saṃdalayatām ||",
              "segment_number": 72,
              "translated_text": "may this great Goddess destroy the fear of worldly existence (<s>bhavabhaya</s>) for me."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 71,
          "translated_text": "having created <s>Yama</s> (death) thus, you then once again shatter doubt —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_19"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vilīne śaṅkaughe sapadi paripūrṇe ca vibhave gate",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "lokācāre galitavibhave śāstraniyame |",
              "segment_number": 74,
              "translated_text": "when worldly convention has passed away and scriptural regulation has lost its power,"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 73,
          "translated_text": "When the flood of doubt has instantly dissolved, and when power has become complete,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "anantaṃ bhogyaughaṃ grasitum abhito laṃpaṭarasā vibho",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "saṃhārākhyā mama hṛdi bhidāṃśaṃ praharatu ||",
              "segment_number": 76,
              "translated_text": "may the [Goddess] named <s>Saṃhāra</s> (dissolution) strike the element of differentiation (<s>bheda</s>) in my heart."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 75,
          "translated_text": "with the relish of passionate eagerness to devour an infinite flood of enjoyments on all sides, O Lord,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_20"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "taditthaṃ devībhiḥ sapadi dalite bhedavibhave",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "vikalpaprāṇāsau pravilasati mātṛsthitir alam |",
              "segment_number": 78,
              "translated_text": "the state of the knower (<s>mātṛsthiti</s>) vibrates fully, its vital breath being conceptualization (<s>vikalpa</s>);"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 77,
          "translated_text": "Thus, when the power of differentiation has been instantly shattered by the Goddesses,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ataḥ saṃhārāṃśam nijahṛdi vimṛśya sthitimayī",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "prasannā syān mṛtyupralayakaraṇī me bhagavatī ||",
              "segment_number": 80,
              "translated_text": "may the Blessed Goddess, who effects the dissolution of death, be gracious [to me]."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 79,
          "translated_text": "therefore, reflecting upon the dissolution-aspect in one's own heart, established in stability,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_21"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "taditthaṃ te tisro nijavibhavavisphāraṇavaśād avāptāḥ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "ṣaṭcakrakramakṛtapadaṃ śaktaya imāḥ |",
              "segment_number": 82,
              "translated_text": "the position created by the sequence of the six <s>cakras</s> (circles),"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 81,
          "translated_text": "Thus these three <s>śaktis</s> (powers) of yours, through the force of manifesting their own glory, having attained"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "kramād unmeṣeṇa pravidadhati citrāṃ bhavadaśām imābhyo",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "devībhyaḥ pravaṇahṛdayaḥ syāṃ gatabhayaḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 84,
              "translated_text": "Goddesses may I be devoted with an inclined heart, freed from fear."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 83,
          "translated_text": "progressively through <s>unmeṣa</s> (blossoming) bring about the variegated condition of existence — toward these"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_22"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "imāṃ rundhe bhūmiṃ bhavabhayabhidātaṅkakaraṇīm imāṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bodhaikāntadrutirasamayīm cāpi vidadhe |",
              "segment_number": 86,
              "translated_text": "she also establishes, consisting entirely of the flowing taste of <s>bodha</s> (awakening);"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 85,
          "translated_text": "She restrains this ground that causes the terror of the fear of existence; this [ground]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "taditthaṃ saṃrodhaṃ drutim atha vilupyāśubhatatīr",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "yatheṣṭaṃ cācāraṃ bhajati lasatāṃ sā mama hṛdi ||",
              "segment_number": 88,
              "translated_text": "she practices conduct as she pleases — may she shine in my heart."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 87,
          "translated_text": "thus, having effected restraint and fluidity, and having destroyed the succession of inauspicious [states],"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_23"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "kriyābuddhyakṣādeḥ parimitapade mānapadavīm avāptasya",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "sphāraṃ nijanijarucā saṃharati yā |",
              "segment_number": 90,
              "translated_text": "she who withdraws the expansion with her own innate radiance —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 89,
          "translated_text": "For one who has attained the path of measurement (<s>māna</s>) in the limited domain of action, cognition, senses, and such,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "iyaṃ mārta.ṅdasya sthitipadayujaḥ sāram akhilam haṭhād",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "ākarṣantī kṛśatu mama bhedaṃ bhavabhayāt ||",
              "segment_number": 92,
              "translated_text": "may she diminish my differentiation (<s>bheda</s>) from the fear of existence."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 91,
          "translated_text": "this one, forcibly extracting the entire essence of the <s>Mārtaṇḍa</s> (Sun), who is endowed with the state of stability,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_24"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "samagrām akṣālīṃ kramavirahitā sātmani muhur",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "niveśyānantāntarbahalitamahāraśminivahā |",
              "segment_number": 94,
              "translated_text": "with floods of great rays intensified endlessly within,"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 93,
          "translated_text": "Without sequence, placing the entire array of senses within herself repeatedly,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "parā divyānandaṃ kalayitum udārādaravatī prasannā me",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bhūyāt hṛdayapadavīṃ bhūṣayatu ca ||",
              "segment_number": 96,
              "translated_text": "to me and adorn the path of my heart."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 95,
          "translated_text": "the supreme [Goddess], eager with noble regard to effect divine bliss (<s>divyānanda</s>), may she be gracious"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_25"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pramāṇe saṃlīne śivapadalasadvaibhavavaśāt",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "śarīraprāṇādir mitakṛtakamātṛsthitimayaḥ |",
              "segment_number": 98,
              "translated_text": "when [the condition] consisting of body, vital breath (<s>prāṇa</s>), and such — the state of limited constructed knower —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 97,
          "translated_text": "When the means of valid knowledge (<s>pramāṇa</s>) has dissolved through the power of the glory shining in the state of <s>Śiva</s>,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yadā kālopādhiḥ pralayapadam āsādayati te tadā devī yāsau",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "lasati mama sā syāc chivamayī ||",
              "segment_number": 100,
              "translated_text": "shines forth — may she become <s>Śiva</s>-natured for me."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 99,
          "translated_text": "when the temporal condition (<s>kālopādhi</s>) attains the state of dissolution in you, then that Goddess who"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_26"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "prakāśākhyā saṃvit kramavirahitā śūnyapadato",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "bahirlīnātyantam prasarati samācchādakatayā |",
              "segment_number": 102,
              "translated_text": "having dissolved externally entirely, spreads forth as the veiling power;"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 101,
          "translated_text": "The consciousness (<s>saṃvid</s>) named <s>Prakāśa</s> (luminosity), without sequence, from the state of void (<s>śūnya</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tato 'py antaḥsāre galitarabhasād akramatayā mahākālī",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "seyaṃ mama kalayatāṃ kālam akhilam ||",
              "segment_number": 104,
              "translated_text": "(Great Goddess of Time), may she effect all of time for me."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 103,
          "translated_text": "then from the inner essence too, having abandoned impetuosity, without sequence — this <s>Mahākālī</s>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_27"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tato devyāṃ yasyāṃ paramaparipūrṇasthitijuṣi kramaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "vicchidyāśu sthitimatirasāt saṃvidadhati |",
              "segment_number": 106,
              "translated_text": "the sequence, effecting [stability] through the excess of the taste for stability,"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 105,
          "translated_text": "Then in that Goddess who is established in the supreme, utterly complete state, quickly cutting"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pramāṇaṃ mātāraṃ mitim atha samagraṃ jagad idaṃ sthitāṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "kroḍīkṛtya śrayatu mama cittaṃ citim imām ||",
              "segment_number": 108,
              "translated_text": "as it stands — may my consciousness resort to this <s>citi</s> (pure awareness)."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 107,
          "translated_text": "having embraced the means of knowledge (<s>pramāṇa</s>), the knower (<s>mātā</s>), the measurement (<s>miti</s>), and this entire world"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_28"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "anargalasvātmamaye maheśe tiṣṭhanti",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "yasmin vibhuśaktayas tāḥ |",
              "segment_number": 110,
              "translated_text": "in whom those all-pervading <s>śaktis</s> abide —"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 109,
          "translated_text": "In that great Lord (<s>Maheśa</s>) who consists of unobstructed Self,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "taṃ śaktimantaṃ praṇamāmi devaṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "manthānasaṃjñaṃ jagadekasāram ||",
              "segment_number": 112,
              "translated_text": "named <s>Manthāna</s> (the Churner), the sole essence of the world."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 111,
          "translated_text": "I bow to that power-possessing God,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "AgKs_29"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "itthaṃ svaśaktikiraṇaughanutiprabandhān ākarṇya deva",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "yadi me vrajasi prasādam |",
              "segment_number": 114,
              "translated_text": "if you bestow grace upon me,"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 113,
          "translated_text": "Having heard this continuous praise composed of the rays of your own <s>śaktis</s>, O God,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tenāśu sarvajanatāṃ",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "lb",
              "attributes": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "nijaśāsanāṃśusaṃśāntitākhilatamaḥpaṭalāṃ vidheyāḥ ||",
              "segment_number": 116,
              "translated_text": "[such that] the entire mass of darkness is pacified by the rays of your teaching."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 115,
          "translated_text": "then quickly make all people"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ṣaṭṣaṣṭinām eke varṣe navamyām asite 'hani |",
          "segment_number": 117,
          "translated_text": "On the ninth day of the dark fortnight of <s>Mārgaśīrṣa</s>, in the year sixty-six,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "mayā 'bhinavaguptena mārgaśīrṣe stutaḥ śivaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 118,
          "translated_text": "<s>Śiva</s> was praised by me, <s>Abhinavagupta</s>."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "iti śrī abhinavaguptapādācāryakṛtaṃ kramastotraṃ sampūrṇam ||",
      "segment_number": 119,
      "translated_text": "Thus the <s>Kramastotra</s> (Hymn of the Krama) composed by the revered master <s>Abhinavagupta</s> is complete."
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "Gandharva-nagaram / DSO Sanskrit Archive"
    }
  ]
}